Method
------
I attacked the Green r7 tokenizer helpers (DISABLE_TEXT_RE and the text
prefilter at scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:902 and :930,
scriptKindForFile at :907, disableCommentRanges at :924,
stripDisableComments at :971, directiveKindsOfFile at :1055) with seeded
files in temp folders under apps/integrated-math-3, each with paired bare
controls. For each form I compared three things: what oxlint honors (a
live probe with the root config), what the pin counts, and what the strip
removes. The probe scripts run the exact helper code of the test file
(transpiled from lines 899-981 and 1047-1073 at HEAD), so the data is the
pipeline's own behavior. About 30 forms over five probe rounds, plus a
49-carrier sweep replica.

Re-check of adv 1 to 12 at this HEAD
-----------------------------------
All pass. Adv 10 (the F1r3 CRLF guard) and adv 11 (the F2r3 in-string /*
guard) now pass live, so the r3 blockers are remediated and both are
withdrawn. The sweep replica over the real tree at this HEAD: 49 carriers,
43 files with surfaced findings, 86 decoded rules, MISSING none, EXTRAS
none, no parse diagnostic.

Attack table (live oxlint behavior vs the tokenizer helpers)
-----------------------------------------------------------
(a) Prefilter spellings. Oxlint does not honor uppercase, mixed case, a
space around the hyphen, or a U+2011 hyphen: each probe exits 1 with the
finding live. The pin counts none of them (the prefilter is
case-sensitive and exact), so the two agree and no hole exists. A BOM at
file start hides nothing from either: oxlint honors the disable, the pin
counts it, and the strip surfaces the finding.
(b) Parse failures and extensions. A file with a syntax error stays loud:
oxlint reports only the parse error (exit 1) and applies no rule finding,
so nothing hides behind a disable there; the pin counts the disable
(conservative) and the stripped copy keeps the parse error. An
unterminated /* comment makes oxlint fail loudly ('Unterminated multiline
comment'); the strip blanks it to EOF, and nothing is lost. A .mts or .cts
file gets no rule from the config globs (a bare control exits 0), so
nothing can hide there; the tokenizer parses and counts them. A .js file
holding JSX lints under oxlint, and a disable in its JSX expression
container is honored exactly as in .tsx; the ScriptKind.JS parse of the
tokenizer finds the comment anyway. A .ts file holding a <number> cast
parses, and the disable above it strips and surfaces.
(c) Positions. A comment-only file counts 1 through the end-of-file
token. A shebang line (in .js and .mjs) hides nothing from either side: a
disable after it is honored, counted, and stripped. A comment inside a
type annotation is honored mid-line. A comment inside a function-body
block and a comment in a JSX attribute position are not honored by oxlint
(the finding stays live) while the pin counts them: the conservative
direction, pinned.
(d) A regex holding disable text (`/eslint-disable/`) is not honored and
not counted: the scanner eats it as one token. A regex holding `\/*`
above a real disable no longer swallows the comment: the disable strips
and the finding surfaces (the F2r3 class, closed).
(e) A template substitution `${/* eslint-disable */ 1}` is honored by
oxlint, counted by the pin, and stripped with the finding surfaced.
(f) Duplicated ranges: a mid-line comment shared by the trivia of two
adjacent tokens counts exactly once (the pos-end dedupe holds).

New coverage
------------
Adv 13 (commit b9a4f0c2) pins the r4 data: group 1 pins each honored form
(shebang .js/.mjs, BOM, .mjs, .cjs, template substitution, the .js JSX
container, the regex-star-slash form, the type-annotation mid-line form,
the deduped adjacent form) with the live honor probe, the pin count, and
the stripped-copy surface; group 2 pins the counted-but-not-honored
shapes (a function-body block, a JSX attribute, an unterminated comment,
a syntax-error file) as staying loud with a conservative count; group 3
pins the unhonored spellings (uppercase, mixed case, a spaced hyphen, a
U+2011 hyphen, regex text) as staying live and uncounted, so a future
oxlint that starts to honor one of them fails the live probe before the
prefilter can go blind.

Findings
--------
No blocking finding. F1r3 and F2r3 are withdrawn (remediated by Green
r7). F4r3 stays accepted as a documented limitation (the strip comment
at scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:964-970 documents it,
and adv 12 pins both fault classes live). Two Nits:

- F1r4 [Nit]: SOURCE_EXT_RE (scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:984)
  hardcodes the extension set of the root config override globs. Live
  probes show .mts and .cts get no rule, so the exclusion is consistent
  today, but nothing ties the two sets: a later glob change that adds
  .mts or .cts would lint those files while the carrier scan stays blind.
  Default: note only.
- F2r4 [Nit]: directiveKindsOfFile classifies a block comment whose text
  merely contains 'disable-line' as trailing
  (scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts:1064-1069), so a blanket
  disable that mentions disable-line in prose adds no blanket block. The
  kinds and count clauses still fail on any change, so no hole exists.
  Default: accept.

